{
  "contract": "ito-chapter-editions",
  "version": 1,
  "notes": [
    "Bytes are postcard. ChapterEditionsRequest is {entry: MediaEntry, cursor: Option<String>, limit: u32 varint}; ChapterEditionsPage is {editions: Vec<Chapter>, next_cursor: Option<String>, scope: CatalogScope, completeness: CatalogCompleteness}. Chapter is the ABI 3 layout pinned by catalog-v3.json; there is no second edition schema.",
    "Entries inside requests use the MediaEntry bytes of catalog-v3.json (variant 0 manga, 1 anime, 2 novel). A request entry reaches the source without chapters or catalog.",
    "An entry with repeat_hex is prefix hex, then repeat_hex repeated repeat_count times, then suffix_hex; entries without it are just hex.",
    "expect is ok, violation:<code>, or decode_error. violation: values for requests are SDK-local classifications; the export reports every bad request as Error::Host with the fixed message request.invalid before source code runs. Page violations are reported as ErrorCategory::ContractViolation with the code as the message.",
    "An entry with canonical_hex is accepted as written; it decodes to the same value as the built case and re-encodes to canonical_hex. Unknown CatalogScope and CatalogCompleteness discriminants decode to Unknown.",
    "Page check order: next_cursor bounds (page.cursor), count against the request limit (page.count), nonterminal completeness (page.completeness), progress (page.no_progress), then the chapter rules of catalog-v3.json (length.*, number.*, duplicate.key, scanlator.conflict). The first violation wins.",
    "A present cursor is 1 to max_cursor_bytes UTF-8 bytes, compared as exact bytes, kept in memory only and never logged. A source binds it to the exact title and the settings, account and filters in effect.",
    "Page validation applies to one page. The host validates across pages: byte-exact key dedupe, metadata and id-name consistency, repeated cursors, constant scope, and the run caps in run_limits. Partial to complete at the last page is valid; complete with a cursor is not."
  ],
  "codes": [
    "request.entry_kind",
    "request.limit",
    "request.cursor",
    "page.cursor",
    "page.count",
    "page.completeness",
    "page.no_progress"
  ],
  "limits": {
    "max_limit": 100,
    "max_cursor_bytes": 4096,
    "max_response_bytes": 16777216
  },
  "run_limits": {
    "max_rows": 20000,
    "max_pages": 256,
    "max_cumulative_bytes": 16777216
  },
